## 5. Your responsibilities

5.1 You must use MeetCap lawfully, and you are responsible for Your Content and for how you use MeetCap. **It is up to you to determine whether your use complies with the laws where you are. We do not guarantee that your use of MeetCap complies with any law or regulation.**

5.2 **Recording others.** You must follow the recording and privacy laws where you are. Before you record a meeting, call or conversation, tell the people involved and get any consent the law requires. Some countries and regions require the consent of every participant.

5.3 **Voiceprints.** Voiceprints are biometric information. Before you save someone else's voiceprint, you must tell them that MeetCap will save it, where it will be kept and how it can be deleted, and obtain their consent as required by applicable law. If they ask you to delete it, you must do so promptly.

5.4 **Content you send to AI.** When you choose to send transcripts or other content to an AI service, you must make sure you are entitled to do so, including by following your organization's rules on meeting content and on sending data outside the organization.

5.5 You may not use MeetCap to unlawfully monitor, eavesdrop on or track anyone, or for any activity that infringes anyone's privacy, trade secrets or other rights.

